1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,700
In India, someone loses their savings to a scam that didn't look like one.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:10,300
A stock tip in a WhatsApp group. A call from “the police”. An app sent as a link.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,500
By the time they realise, the money is already gone,

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,050
because UPI payments cannot be undone.

5
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:19,370
I am Geeta, and this is Tripwire.

6
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:25,650
It follows a scam as it unfolds, across WhatsApp, Telegram, SMS, calls and payments,

7
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:30,150
and stops you at the one moment that matters: right before you pay.

8
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,250
Let me show you.

9
00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:32,350
Last year,

10
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:33,310
Indians lost over

11
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:36,337
₹22,000 crore to cyber fraud.

12
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:38,090
Three of every four rupees

13
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:39,877
were never recovered.

14
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,280
Because a scam isn't one message.

15
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,920
It's a script that plays out over days,

16
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,200
across apps.

17
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,073
And no single app sees all of it.

18
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:50,860
Meet Tripwire.

19
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:53,640
A stranger promises guaranteed returns.

20
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,540
Tripwire is already reading the pattern,

21
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,794
quietly, on the phone.

22
00:00:57,910 --> 00:00:59,910
Then comes an app link.

23
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:02,650
Each step is matched against how

24
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:04,980
real investment scams unfold.

25
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:07,120
When the install screen opens,

26
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,400
Tripwire steps in before

27
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,440
the app is installed,

28
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,921
not after.

29
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:14,320
One tap, and the install is cancelled.

30
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,810
And at the moment of payment,

31
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:20,570
it shows exactly why: what happened,

32
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:22,940
in order, and a hard fact.

33
00:01:23,270 --> 00:01:24,690
Registered brokers must

34
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:27,920
use a SEBI @valid address.

35
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:29,543
This one doesn't.

36
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:31,090
It never blocks you.

37
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:32,370
You can still go ahead,

38
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:34,492
but only on purpose.

39
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:36,380
A code arrives while a

40
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:38,000
stranger is on the line?

41
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,400
Tripwire warns you not to share it,

42
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,753
without ever reading the code.

43
00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:44,350
A fake “money credited”

44
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,990
message from a mobile number?

45
00:01:45,990 --> 00:01:49,587
Flagged. Banks never send from one.

46
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:51,470
Phone checkup finds apps

47
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:53,230
that can steal your codes,

48
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:55,275
and helps you remove them.

49
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,300
If an app from a link grabs

50
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,980
control of your screen,

51
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:01,907
Tripwire raises the alarm instantly.

52
00:02:02,010 --> 00:02:04,370
Warnings in Hindi or English,

53
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:06,710
read aloud for those who need it.

54
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:09,140
If money is already gone,

55
00:02:09,390 --> 00:02:10,550
every minute counts.

56
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:12,310
Tripwire starts the clock,

57
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:16,126
calls 1930 and your bank's fraud line,

58
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:19,820
and builds the complaint pack in seconds.

59
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:23,480
Scammers change their words every day,

60
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:25,520
so keyword rules miss a lot,

61
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:28,020
especially in Hindi and Hinglish.

62
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:31,176
That's why we built our own AI model.

63
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,240
It reads each message and

64
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,290
names the trick being used:

65
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:37,880
a promise of guaranteed returns,

66
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,160
pressure to act now,

67
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,266
or a request to keep it secret.

68
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:44,760
First, we defined 14 scam tactics,

69
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,360
with a clear rule for

70
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,292
when each one applies.

71
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:50,390
Then we built a dataset

72
00:02:50,390 --> 00:02:51,850
of 15,000 messages,

73
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:54,270
in English, Hindi and Hinglish,

74
00:02:54,270 --> 00:02:56,410
both scam and everyday,

75
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:58,323
each labelled with its tactics.

76
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:01,220
We trained an open model, Qwen 2.5,

77
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,180
with half a billion parameters,

78
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:04,040
on a laptop,

79
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:06,577
using a technique called LoRA.

80
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:09,130
Then we compressed it into a single

81
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:10,930
file built for Android phones,

82
00:03:10,930 --> 00:03:14,391
so messages never have to leave the phone.

83
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:17,130
On messages it had never seen,

84
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:19,470
it nearly doubled our Hindi detection.

85
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:21,870
And when we replayed scam conversations,

86
00:03:21,870 --> 00:03:24,310
it caught all six before the payment,

87
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:26,600
with no false warnings.

88
00:03:26,990 --> 00:03:29,130
Now we're cutting its false

89
00:03:29,130 --> 00:03:31,330
alarms on everyday messages,

90
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:33,230
with real chats,

91
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:34,590
personal details removed,

92
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:36,950
and Google's larger Gemma models,

93
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:41,180
before we switch it on for everyone.

94
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:44,200
Already, when a warning fires,

95
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,560
Tripwire prepares a text

96
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,120
to a trusted person,

97
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,621
ready to send.

98
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,450
And this is where Tripwire is going.

99
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,520
When a warning fires on Mum's phone,

100
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,280
her son is alerted instantly,

101
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,680
with the type of scam

102
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,300
and how far it has got,

103
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:02,210
never her messages.

104
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:04,150
Before a big payment

105
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,810
to a stranger goes out,

106
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:07,510
he approves it or stops it,

107
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:09,357
from his own phone.

108
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:12,480
And every warning speaks her language:

109
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:15,360
Hindi, Telugu, Tamil, Bengali,

110
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,852
Marathi and more.

111
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:17,840
Tripwire.

112
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,888
Stops the scam before the payment.
